mapping "H480B.1" source="H480B" target="76976005" relationship=source_is_narrower_than_target {
    confidence 0.03 scheme="vocabmod-se-confidence@1"
    comment "en" """
        Source H480B SNOMED CT 76976005 = optic atrophy due to intracranial neoplasm — the source bundles
        optic atrophy with an intracranial neoplasm cause. No SNOMED CT standard concept for this exact
        combination exists in the mirror. Target SNOMED CT 372914 (76976005), the standard concept that
        subsumes the optic-atrophy axis of the source (broader). The neoplasm-cause axis is dropped. Low
        confidence : the target captures the primary clinical finding but loses the etiology.
        """
}
mapping "H480C.1" source="H480C" target="76976005" relationship=source_is_narrower_than_target {
    confidence 0.03 scheme="vocabmod-se-confidence@1"
    comment "en" """
        Source H480C SNOMED CT 76976005 = optic atrophy due to other intracranial disorder. As with H480B,
        no exact standard concept exists. Target SNOMED CT 372914 (76976005), the parent that subsumes the
        optic-atrophy axis (broader). Etiology is dropped; low.
        """
}
mapping "H480W.1" source="H480W" target="76976005" relationship=source_is_narrower_than_target {
    confidence 0.71 scheme="vocabmod-se-confidence@1"
    comment "en" """
        Source H480W SNOMED CT 76976005 = optic atrophy in diseases classified elsewhere (residual bucket).
